==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s (1,200%) spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Snache]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.
**1 [[Bore]] spawns.

==Strategy==
You don't need any Anti-Red Ubers for this stage. If you have [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], all you need to do is send multiple of them out to alternate attacks and keep the Bores frozen forever. It could perhaps be tried with non-100% Red Freeze Units. The main threat will be the Gories and Hippoes unless you've got a few other Cats in the team to deal with them. Without them, stack [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Captain Cats]], [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Sorceress Cat]]s, [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cats]]/Cyborg Cats and meatshields. The Captain Cats should knock back the Bores while the Sorceress Cats should be able to slow them and stall until your Captain Cats can knock them back again. The Paris Cats should be able to hit the base, but you can also send in [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or any other high-damage cats to do so as well.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] with a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies should do well here. Most [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] Ubers like [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]] or [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]] do especially well here, so keep that in mind. Below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Cat]]: No Bore can stand against her sheer [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controlling]] power.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: It is recommended to only use the [[True Form]] of this cat for this stage, as the other forms are quite lacking. Their [[Wave Attack]]s effect all the Bores, but works best when they are somewhat [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controlled]] so they can utilize their full DPS.
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]]: A no brainer. Makes the stage a joke.
*[[Tropical Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Tropical Kalisa]]: Powerful [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] that can [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|nuke]] the Bores with her [[Massive Damage|massive damage]]
*[[Raiden (Uber Rare Cat)|Raiden]]: His constant [[Knockback|knockback]] keeps the Bores at bay, while doing consistent damage to them.
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]]: Same as Tropical Kalisa, minus being a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]].
*[[The White Rabbit (Uber Rare Cat)|The White Rabbit]]: Another powerful [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controller]]. Stands at a safe range while [[Slow|slowing]] the Bores from a distance.

